Whole-artifact consistency and requirement coverage","selectors":[],"concerns":["Cross-check all LLD contracts, error paths, tests, diagrams, migration steps, and UX against one another and the originating issue.","Identify omitted requirements, contradictions, feasibility or dependency-order problems, and any remaining scope gaps."],"dependsOn":["store-write","protocol-host","document-editor","sequence-and-alternatives","citations-context"],"purpose":"consistency"}],"coverageExplanation":"Inventory units are assigned to substantive chunks by implementation responsibility and traceability; shared contract, error, migration, and test sections are intentionally reviewed alongside both store and host/view responsibilities. The final consistency chunk depends on every substantive chunk and checks end-to-end alignment with the originating issue.","finalConsistencyChunkId":"consistency","coverage":[{"unitId":"/body/adherence","chunkIds":["sequence-and-alternatives"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered","chunkIds":["sequence-and-alternatives"]},{"unitId":"/body/chosenAlternative","chunkIds":["sequence-and-alternatives"]},{"unitId":"/body/contractDetails","chunkIds":["store-write","protocol-host","document-editor"]},{"unitId":"/body/dataModelChanges","chunkIds":["store-write","protocol-host","document-editor"]},{"unitId":"/body/errorPaths","chunkIds":["store-write","protocol-host","document-editor"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice","chunkIds":["sequence-and-alternatives"]},{"unitId":"/body/interactionWithShared","chunkIds":["sequence-and-alternatives"]},{"unitId":"/body/migration","chunkIds":["store-write","protocol-host","document-editor"]},{"unitId":"/body/openQuestions","chunkIds":["citations-context"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition","chunkIds":["sequence-and-alternatives"]},{"unitId":"/body/summary","chunkIds":["citations-context"]},{"unitId":"/body/testStrategy","chunkIds":["store-write","protocol-host","document-editor"]},{"unitId":"/body/uxDefinition","chunkIds":["document-editor"]},{"unitId":"/body/companions","chunkIds":["citations-context"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","chunkIds":["sequence-and-alternatives"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","chunkIds":["sequence-and-alternatives"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","chunkIds":["sequence-and-alternatives"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/3","chunkIds":["sequence-and-alternatives"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","chunkIds":["sequence-and-alternatives"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","chunkIds":["sequence-and-alternatives"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","chunkIds":["sequence-and-alternatives"]},{"unitId":"/body/uxDefinition/body/1/items/0/columns/0/items/0","chunkIds":["document-editor"]},{"unitId":"/citations/0","chunkIds":["citations-context"]},{"unitId":"/citations/1","chunkIds":["citations-context"]},{"unitId":"/citations/2","chunkIds":["citations-context"]},{"unitId":"/citations/3","chunkIds":["citations-context"]},{"unitId":"/citations/4","chunkIds":["citations-context"]},{"unitId":"/citations/5","chunkIds":["citations-context"]},{"unitId":"document:line:26","chunkIds":["citations-context"]},{"unitId":"document:line:179","chunkIds":["sequence-and-alternatives"]},{"unitId":"document:line:294","chunkIds":["document-editor"]}]},"unitSummaries":[{"unitId":"planning","phase":"planning","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"store-write","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"protocol-host","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"document-editor","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"sequence-and-alternatives","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"citations-context","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"review-lld-01ac1e4b6a6c9c2f-s1","attempt":1,"artifactId":"LLD-01ac1e4b6a6c9c2f-s1","status":"incomplete","counts":{"HIGH":0,"MED":4,"LOW":0},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"store-write","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The LLD traces the store update to the issue and specifies replacement, validation, metadata refresh, cleanup, and failure tests. However, the proposed temp-file creation does not specify exclusive/no-follow creation, so the stated filesystem safety is not established against a pre-existing temp-path symlink; the named fake also does not currently model rename or exclusive creation.","findings":[{"id":"store-temp-safety","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges, ScratchStore interface update (LLD.md §3.2)","message":"The update path writes to a predictable `<root>/.tmp-<pid>-<random>` path, but the contract does not require exclusive creation or no-follow behavior. The existing node adapter uses `writeFile(path, data)` without exclusive flags, which follows a pre-existing symlink; if that temp name is occupied by a symlink, the save could write outside the scratch root before publication fails or proceeds. The safety claim therefore needs an exclusive temp-file contract (and corresponding production adapter and test fake coverage).","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §3.2 and §7 step 1: temp file is specified as pid+random suffix and written, with no exclusive/no-follow creation requirement.","vscode-plugin/src/chat/scratch-store.ts: ScratchFs.writeFile(path, data) and nodeScratchFs.writeFile delegates to writeFile(p, data) without exclusive flags.","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/fake-scratch-fs.ts: writeFile directly puts bytes at the path and models no symlink-following or exclusive-create semantics.","ISSUE.md, Fix intent: requires an atomic and safely rewritten file preserving store invariants."]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/migration","/body/testStrategy","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/scratchpad-document-view-read-only-cannot-E2026111401ac1e4b/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/scratchpad-document-view-read-only-cannot-E2026111401ac1e4b/ISSUE.md","vscode-plugin/src/chat/scratch-store.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/fake-scratch-fs.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/scratch-store.test.ts","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/review-lld-01ac1e4b6a6c9c2f-s1.json"],"limitations":[],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"protocol-host","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The LLD aligns the save intent with the existing scratch router and specifies runtime string checks, direction-specific protocol registration, failure replies, and browse/chat-list refresh. One contract inconsistency blocks implementation: the reply is required to be generation-guarded, but neither the save intent nor the reply carries a generation, and the existing ScratchPanels API does not expose a generation-correlated reply operation.","findings":[{"id":"save-reply-generation-contract","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails, §2.3 scratch-saved reply and §2.5 scratch-save route","message":"The reply contract requires stale replies to be ignored by matching a generation tag, but the declared scratch-saved shape contains only id, ok, and optional error; the scratch-save intent likewise carries only id and text. The current controller tracks docGeneration internally and routes incoming scratch-ready messages using their gen, but ScratchPanels exposes no operation for posting a save result to the currently displayed document generation. As written, implementers cannot satisfy both the reply shape and the generation-guard requirement. Define where the generation is captured/carried and how the host targets the live panel, or revise the stale-reply guarantee and contract consistently.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §2.2 declares scratch-save as { type, id, text } with no generation field.","LLD.md §2.3 declares scratch-saved as { type, id, ok, error? }, then requires matching id+current generation and states the generation tag is echoed in scratch-saved.","LLD.md §2.5 routes the reply to the document panel, but the existing ScratchPanels interface has no save-reply method.","vscode-plugin/src/panels/scratch-panels.ts: openDocument captures docGeneration internally; its webview callback validates gen for scratch-ready, while ScratchPanels only exposes openDocument, refreshBrowse, closeDocumentIfShowing, invalidateId, showingId, and dispose.","vscode-plugin/src/chat/scratch-host.ts: ScratchHostDeps receives ScratchPanels and the current router handles scratch intents; it has no direct document-generation value."]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/migration","/body/testStrategy","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/scratchpad-document-view-read-only-cannot-E2026111401ac1e4b/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/scratchpad-document-view-read-only-cannot-E2026111401ac1e4b/ISSUE.md","vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/scratch-host.ts","vscode-plugin/src/panels/scratch-panels.ts","vscode-plugin/src/panels/__tests__/scratch-panel.test.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/protocol.test.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/extension-chat-wiring.test.ts","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/review-lld-01ac1e4b6a6c9c2f-s1.json"],"limitations":[],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"document-editor","status":"incomplete","summary":"The LLD traces the editable view, save affordances, error feedback, and send-to-chat behavior to the originating issue, and the UX mock source describes clean, dirty, saved, and failed states. The proposed send-to-chat behavior is not compatible with the textarea selection API as currently specified, and rendered UX verification was unavailable. Prior checkpoint feedback also identifies an unresolved generation-correlation gap in the save reply contract.","findings":[{"id":"textarea-selection-api","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails §2.4 and §3.3; /body/testStrategy ac5","message":"The design changes the selected content surface from a <pre> to a <textarea> but says to keep the existing selectionchange logic unchanged. That logic reads window.getSelection().toString(); selections inside a textarea are exposed through the textarea’s selectionStart/selectionEnd and are not returned as a DOM Range selection. Consequently, the floating Send-to-chat action may no longer capture selected textarea text, contradicting the issue’s requirement to preserve selection-based sending. Specify textarea-selection handling and test the actual textarea selection path.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §2.4 and §3.3: the content surface becomes a textarea while selectionchange send-to-chat logic is to remain unchanged.","vscode-plugin/src/panels/scratch-panels.ts: documentBootstrap reads window.getSelection().toString() in its selectionchange handler.","vscode-plugin/src/panels/__tests__/scratch-panel.test.ts: existing selection test supplies window.getSelection() with a synthetic selection string and uses a pre stub, so it does not exercise textarea selectionStart/selectionEnd.","ISSUE.md Fix intent: explicitly requires selection-based floating Send-to-chat behavior to keep working on the editable surface."]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/migration","/body/testStrategy","/body/uxDefinition","/body/uxDefinition/body/1/items/0/columns/0/items/0","document:line:294","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/scratchpad-document-view-read-only-cannot-E2026111401ac1e4b/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/scratchpad-document-view-read-only-cannot-E2026111401ac1e4b/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/scratchpad-document-view-read-only-cannot-E2026111401ac1e4b/S001/ux-mock.html (source inspected; rendered appearance not verified)","vscode-plugin/src/panels/scratch-panels.ts","vscode-plugin/src/panels/__tests__/scratch-panel.test.ts","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/review-lld-01ac1e4b6a6c9c2f-s1.json"],"limitations":["Could not inspect the UX mock’s actual rendering: the computer/browser host was unavailable. The HTML source was inspected, but it does not establish visual layout/rendering.","The checkpoint records an unresolved MED finding, save-reply-generation-contract, that the scratch-save/reply shapes omit generation correlation even though the LLD requires stale-generation replies to be ignored; this assignment did not re-review or verify a resolution to that issue."],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"sequence-and-alternatives","status":"incomplete","summary":"The selected alternative directly addresses the issue’s in-plugin editing request and preserves the existing scratchpad view and store boundary. The sequence captures the main save round-trip, but the design’s claim that send-to-chat selection works unchanged over a textarea conflicts with the current implementation. The diagram’s rendered appearance could not be verified because the browser host was unavailable.","findings":[{"id":"sequence-textarea-selection","severity":"MED","location":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0, pros; /body/sequenceDefinition, final message note","message":"The chosen alternative claims the existing selection code works over textarea selections and the sequence says that path runs unchanged. The current document bootstrap reads window.getSelection(), but textarea selections are exposed through selectionStart/selectionEnd rather than a DOM Range selection. This makes the diagram and alternative rationale inconsistent with the implemented selection API and the issue’s preservation requirement. Specify textarea selection handling and update the sequence and tests accordingly.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md §2.4 and §3.3 require the selectionchange logic to remain unchanged after replacing the <pre> with a <textarea>.","LLD.md §8 alternative a1 says the existing send-to-chat selection code works on textarea selections; sequenceDefinition notes it runs in parallel unchanged.","vscode-plugin/src/panels/scratch-panels.ts: documentBootstrap obtains selected text with window.getSelection().toString().","ISSUE.md fix intent requires selection-based send-to-chat to keep working on the editable surface."]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/adherence","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/hldContextSlice","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/alternativesConsidered/3","document:line:179","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/scratchpad-document-view-read-only-cannot-E2026111401ac1e4b/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/scratchpad-document-view-read-only-cannot-E2026111401ac1e4b/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/scratchpad-document-view-read-only-cannot-E2026111401ac1e4b/S001/sequence-diagram.html (source inspected; rendering not verified)","vscode-plugin/src/panels/scratch-panels.ts","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/review-lld-